11. The biggest strategic recommendation
There is something I want to emphasize.

You're building a personal portfolio as a B.Tech CSE (AI/ML) student.

Your website should demonstrate three things:
1. Engineering ability: You understand architecture, algorithms, performance and implementation.
2. Problem-solving ability: You can identify problems, make technical decisions and explain trade-offs.
3. Personal identity: Your website has a recognizable design language and feels like your own work.
The Fluid Lab can demonstrate the first two exceptionally well.

But it should complement your projects, not replace them.

I would rather see a portfolio with:
- Four genuinely interesting projects.
- Excellent technical case studies.
- Two distinctive themes.
- A polished, custom WorksWheel.
- One exceptionally well-engineered Fluid Lab.
Than a portfolio with 30 different animations and insufficient substance behind them.

The best technical portfolio isn't the one with the most complicated technology. It's the one where every technical decision has a clear reason to exist.